"comparison": "Both Citigroup (C) and JPMorgan Chase (JPM) consolidate specific conduit structures (ABCP conduits for C, multi-seller conduits for JPM) based on their roles as administrators or administrative agents, which provides them with the power to direct significant activities and creates a potentially significant economic interest through fees and liquidity facilities. Specifically, C states it consolidates because 'through its roles as administrator and liquidity provider, it has both the power to direct the activities that most significantly impact the entities' economic performance and an economic interest that could potentially be significant' (c_2024_8_P678_S002). Similarly, JPM consolidates its conduits 'as the Firm has both the power to direct the significant activities of the conduits and a potentially significant economic interest' (jpm_2024_8_P627_S001), noting that 'As administrative agent and in its role in structuring transactions, the Firm makes decisions regarding asset types and credit quality, and manages the commercial paper funding needs of the conduits' (jpm_2024_8_P627_S002).",
